{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5a21fe18-797d-48ed-b2e2-eb92d7a879df",
    "name": "Piqnex Admin API",
    "version": "1.7.0",
    "description": "piqnex-backend (NestJS + Prisma) - the Admin Dashboard's API only: its own dedicated login (independent of the regular user login), moderating listings/need requests, managing users and their roles, and managing the categories/brands catalog.\n\nThis used to be one folder inside a combined collection together with the regular user-facing endpoints (see Piqnex-User-API.postman_collection.json for those - split out on 2026-10-03 so the two APIs can be versioned and maintained independently; see each collection's own CHANGELOG for history before and after the split).\n\nEvery request here needs {{accessToken}} to belong to a user with is_admin = true. There's no API to promote a user - after signing up (via the User API collection), set it directly in the DB, e.g.:\n\nUPDATE users SET is_admin = true, role = 'ADMIN' WHERE email = 'you@example.com';\n\n(or `npx prisma studio` -> users table - role is 'ADMIN' or 'MODERATOR'). Then run 'Auth > Admin Login' (POST /admin/auth/login) - it automatically saves {{accessToken}} the same way the User API's 'Log in' does, and every other request here already uses Bearer {{accessToken}} at the collection level.\n\nTwo admin roles, both gated by is_admin = true but split further by the role column:\n- ADMIN: everything in this collection.\n- MODERATOR: only the Listings and Need Requests folders - Users & Roles and every Catalog request return 403 for a Moderator (see RolesGuard / @Roles('ADMIN') in admin.controller.ts).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
